🔼 Vertical Scaling (Scale Up)
Increases the capacity of a single machine by upgrading its hardware or software resources.
Also known as: Scale Up
Implementation: Easy to implement
Communication: Network calls (RPC)
Examples: MySQL, Amazon RDS

✅ Advantages
Increases individual capacity
Easier to manage

❌ Disadvantages
Limited scalability
Increased cost with high-end hardware
Single point of failure

🔁 Horizontal Scaling (Scale Out)
Involves adding more machines (nodes) to distribute the load.
Also known as: Scale Out
Implementation: More complex
Communication: Inter-process communication
Examples: Cassandra, MongoDB, Gmail, YouTube, Yahoo

✅ Advantages
Increased capacity
Improved performance
Enhanced fault tolerance
Reduces risk of single point of failure

❌ Disadvantages
Expensive setup
Increased operational complexity and cost
